This idea, slightly revised, has enough merit to be
worth dragging out to a separately titled thread,
though I'd like to change the decay criterion from
"wall clock time" to "generations as a bones file".

The level with four bones stacks on it is fairly
rare, but it is even more of a time-munching
nuisance and balance destroying mess; anything that
culls objects to lessen the burden of BUC IDing it
all and testing / IDing it all, and from turning the
game into a Monty-Haul mess, would be a help.

Perhaps "decaying away", say, 25% of the bones
files' contents [where "standing on a grave" ==
"bones file" as a first cut, though some bones
files, like ones on stairs, don't _have_ graves,
IIUC, so maybe a break with save file compatibility
to mark objects permanently as "bones stack derived"
would be needed] on a level, with each time a level
is saved as a bones file, would be a good rate of
decay, including the first such save. The latter
would be a good deterrant to "bones stuffing".

